---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import avatar from '../assets/about/avatar.jpg';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="About" description="About Érico Perez Neto">
  <section class="section-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stack-32">
        <h1 class="h-display">About</h1>

        <div class="stack-16">
          <span class="label">Background</span>
          <div class="about-bio content-width">
            <Image
              src={avatar}
              alt="Érico Perez Neto"
              width={240}
              height={240}
              class="about-avatar"
            />
            <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
              I’m Érico, a Staff Engineer based in São Paulo. I’ve been writing software for 30
              years, with the last 16 dedicated to Apple platforms — primarily iOS apps in
              environments where stability isn’t optional (banking, payments, fintech), reaching
              tens of millions of users. More recently I’ve also been contributing to open source,
              writing command-line tools for Swift codebases — available for macOS and Linux.
            </p>
            <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
              That work made me serious about the small stuff — test discipline, code organization,
              the habit of catching weak assertions before they ship. The <a
                href="/open-source/"
                class="link-inline">open source CLIs</a
              > you’ll find here grew out of problems I kept running into: measuring test effectiveness
              honestly, surfacing structural duplication, and enforcing a predictable shape for Swift
              types.
            </p>
            <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
              Most of my work has been at Staff and Principal levels at companies like Itaú Rede,
              Creditas, ThoughtWorks, and PagSeguro. At Rede in particular, alongside mobile
              architecture, I designed the backend contracts and integrations that mobile clients
              depend on — work that made me think about the API and the device as one system, not
              two.
            </p>
            <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
              This site is where I share what I build and write about what I learn along the way.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a href="/contact/" class="link-arrow self-start"
          >Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
